  "description": "INULAH crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C169 H149 Er7 N6 O34,4(C1 H1 Cl3),2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er4 (Er) has 6 O neighbors; Er1A (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er3A (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er4A (Er) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 8 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.744-3.815 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 106.89-111.92°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Er7(L)2(LH)4(dbm)5(OH)2(CH3OH)4]·4CHCl3·2H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
